# id: M78-read-answered-outside-its-extent
# expect: killed
# covering-test: TestAReadIsReroutedWhenItsRangeNoLongerHoldsTheKey
# package: ./store/
# power-covered-by: TestAReadIsReroutedWhenItsRangeNoLongerHoldsTheKey -- a DIRECTED test. This class is a WINDOW rather than a state: a read routed to the range that owned its key and answered after that range split the key away. A sweep reaches it on about one seed in twenty-seven (8 detections in 200 seeds) and this reaches it every time. The measured field rate that produced BUG-026 was 526 of 25,000 exit-run seeds, 2.10%
# power-refutation: this class named TestRaftExitCriteria when it was declared -- a 10,000-seed sweep, 19 hours per invocation at the exit run's measured 6.9 s/seed. Seven mutants named it, so make mutants asked for six days of machine time for that covering test alone, and make mutants is in the ci target. Declaring a sweep as a covering test is the disease this phase diagnosed twice and then reproduced four times while writing the general form
# mutates: the extent check at the ANSWER site is removed, so a read-index read queued on a range that has since split the key away is answered from that range's state instead of being rerouted. This is BUG-026 exactly, and it is the first member of the read-is-a-log-entry class to be planted: the replicated path gets this check for free because a read is an ENTRY there -- it applies at a position, the apply loop asks desc.Contains like it does for every other command, and an entry outside the extent goes to rerouteAt. Read index has no entry, reaches no apply, and so reached no check. The answer it produces is 'not found', which is the absence of a RANGE delivered to a client as the absence of a VALUE. Note what makes this class hard to instrument: the range's own committed log at that position genuinely no longer holds the key, so the live answer and a replay of the log AGREE, and an oracle that compares them is silent. It is killed by read-index-answers-match-the-log only because that oracle was given a third half -- ownership -- which is a fact serveReadyReads needed and did not take
